          "title": "You'll want to know: коллекционировать",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "коллекционировать (kollektsionírovat) — \"to collect (as a hobby)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Мой сосед коллекционирует старые монеты. Moy soséd kollektsioníruyet stáryye monéty. My neighbour collects old coins."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Imperfective; present коллекционирую."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "коллекционировать (kollektsionírovat) is built on коллекция 'a collection', a learned borrowing usually traced to Latin collēctiō 'a collecting together' (Lewis & Short), from colligere; EtymDB lists the verb without a source."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
